import json,html,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
from quality_gate import calibration_gate
B=Path(__file__).parent;R=B.parent.parent
checks=json.loads((B/'full-checks.json').read_text());run=json.loads((B/'full-run.json').read_text())
gate=calibration_gate(json.loads((B/'calibration-eval_results.json').read_text()),json.loads((B/'calibration.json').read_text()))
(B/'calibration-gates.json').write_text(json.dumps(gate,indent=2))
counts={k:sum(bool(x[k]) for x in checks) for k in ['completed','tool_selection','boundary_behavior','citation_provenance']}
summary={'deployment':'01f1e460818a1da1b370b6a4e47f76ca','unit_tests':186,'deployed_checks':'18/18','client_checks':'12 policy + 7 citation + 4 privacy-trace + 5 citation-repair','refusal_controls':'16/16','calibration_gate_controls':'5/5','followup':counts,'raw_mlflow':run,'judge_calibration':gate,'extra_calls_outside_original_allowed_sets':[{ 'id':c['id'],'tools':c['out_of_scope_calls']} for c in checks if c['out_of_scope_calls']],'live_citation_repair':json.loads((B/'citation-live-repair.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')),'client_sha256':hashlib.sha256((R/'test-mcp-chat.ps1').read_bytes()).hexdigest()}
(B/'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
url='https://dbc-aae0ba16-8727.cloud.databricks.com/ml/experiments/1096079759942705/runs/'+run['run_id']
body=f'''<!doctype html><html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>MCP fixes and verification</title><style>body{{font:17px Arial;line-height:1.5;max-width:1000px;margin:40px auto;color:#173047}}h1,h2{{color:#001970}}td,th{{padding:10px;border:1px solid #ccd8e0;text-align:left}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}}th{{background:#17467d;color:white}}</style><h1>Mother–Child Pharmacology MCP: fixes verified</h1><p>November 19, 2026. Original experiment results remain unchanged.</p><table><tr><th>Change</th><th>Verification</th></tr><tr><td>Negated dosing exclusions</td><td>“Do not give a dose” allows research; separate personal dosing, urgent and identity requests remain blocked. Ten new wording regression cases.</td></tr><tr><td>Citation delivery</td><td>One bounded model repair, then the same strict catalog validation. Unknown IDs/URLs remain rejected. Five local checks and a live deliberately corrupted citation passed.</td></tr><tr><td>Relevance disclosure</td><td>Tool results identify literal match fields and missing topic words. Chat separates broader notices and related-outcome trials from direct topic fit. Study type is returned from registry metadata.</td></tr><tr><td>Refusal evaluation</td><td>Approved fixed text plus zero downstream calls checked deterministically. Sixteen positive/negative controls passed.</td></tr><tr><td>Judge reliability</td><td>Calibration gates prevent an unreliable judge from being treated as an acceptance authority. Five gate tests passed.</td></tr></table><h2>Results</h2><p>186 Python tests and 18 deployed checks passed. All 10 follow-up chats completed, with 10/10 required-tool selection, 10/10 expected boundary behavior and 10/10 citation provenance. The earlier registry failure also passed a separate parent-inventory follow-up.</p><p><a href="{url}">Completed MLflow follow-up</a>: evidence fidelity v2 10/10; task fulfillment v2 9/10. Each includes two deterministic approved-refusal checks; eight research responses used model judges. These scores use a revised evaluator and must not be presented as directly comparable clinical-accuracy improvements over the old experiment.</p><h2>Calibration and remaining limitations</h2><p>Four synthetic fixtures included correct and deliberately incorrect observation/monitoring summaries and deadline statements. Evidence-fidelity judge matched 4/4; task-fulfillment judge matched 3/4, falsely rejecting a correct unknown-deadline statement. Its task scores are therefore diagnostic-only. The task judge also flagged E06 despite the answer explicitly labeling broad notices and unknown deadlines; the original flag is retained.</p><p>The follow-up made three calls outside the original predefined relevance sets: search_literature and get_patient_education in E01, and get_patient_education in E08. They did not prevent task completion but show that efficiency still varies. No broad claim that extra tool calls are eliminated is made.</p><p>Heuristic routing is incomplete, literal topic matching is not clinical suitability, and citation repair cannot certify factual accuracy. No clinician certification or production-readiness claim. Further independent review remains necessary.</p><h2>Reproducibility</h2><p>Deployment: {summary['deployment']}. Cases are unchanged from the initial ten-question pilot. Server deployed with the existing bundle and no new resources. Client changes are local companion code. Original failures and baseline runs are preserved in ../selection-explanation/. This directory retains follow-up captures, scorer version, calibration fixtures/gates, local controls and summary.json. Early scoring attempts failed on null expectation metadata; those attempts are archived as schema-attempt files, not counted as completed results.</p></html>'''
(B/'report.html').write_text(body,encoding='utf-8')
print(json.dumps({'counts':counts,'calibration':gate,'run_id':run['run_id']}))

